1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,780
If your knee replacement still hurts

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:05,430
and the X-ray keeps coming back fine,

3
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:06,810
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:08,090
I've run heavy equipment

5
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:09,790
for thirty-two years.

6
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:10,890
Climbing in and out of

7
00:00:10,890 --> 00:00:12,910
that cab and bouncing around in

8
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:14,890
the seat all day long.

9
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:15,720
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,570
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:17,570 --> 00:00:19,740
It has hurt every day since.

12
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,190
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:22,880
I know what that felt like,

14
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:23,950
and it went away.

15
00:00:23,950 --> 00:00:25,080
This is different.

16
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:25,870
Tight.

17
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:26,480
Full.

18
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,360
Like a band around

19
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,730
the joint that never loosens.

20
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:31,000
And for two years

21
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,430
I've been told the same thing.

22
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:33,470
Give it time.

23
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:35,600
At six weeks it was swelling,

24
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,950
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:38,170
At three months,

26
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,240
give it six.

27
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:40,320
At six months,

28
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:42,220
some knees take a full year.

29
00:00:42,220 --> 00:00:43,050
At a year,

30
00:00:43,050 --> 00:00:45,290
eighteen months isn't unusual.

31
00:00:45,290 --> 00:00:46,520
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:47,820
We went down the list.

33
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:49,600
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,720
Every session,

35
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,490
every exercise at home.

36
00:00:52,490 --> 00:00:53,470
I got stronger.

37
00:00:53,470 --> 00:00:54,970
The tightness never moved.

38
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:56,380
The pain pills helped,

39
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:57,890
and that was the problem.

40
00:00:57,890 --> 00:00:59,900
I'm already on enough every morning,

41
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:00,850
and nobody could tell me

42
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:02,180
when I'd get to stop.

43
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:03,490
Then a nerve block.

44
00:01:03,490 --> 00:01:05,250
Then talk of burning the nerve.

45
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:06,360
And after that, a second

46
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:07,410
operation to go back

47
00:01:07,410 --> 00:01:08,480
in and do it over.

48
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:09,620
I said no.

49
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:11,400
Every morning I stepped out of bed

50
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:12,250
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:13,970
a band was wrapped around it,

52
00:01:13,970 --> 00:01:17,110
tightening every inch I tried to straighten.

53
00:01:17,110 --> 00:01:18,520
Every morning I took something

54
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,380
for it and went to work.

55
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,870
Couldn't do the stairs,

56
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:22,920
couldn't stand at the counter

57
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,590
long enough to finish dinner,

58
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:26,070
couldn't sit through my granddaughter's

59
00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:28,330
game without shifting every two minutes.

60
00:01:28,330 --> 00:01:29,800
At work, I couldn't pull

61
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,410
myself up into the cab without

62
00:01:31,410 --> 00:01:33,100
both hands on the rail.

63
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:34,560
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,930
and it turned ordinary things,

65
00:01:36,930 --> 00:01:38,230
like getting in the truck

66
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:39,660
or up off the couch,

67
00:01:39,660 --> 00:01:40,960
into a decision.

68
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,280
After a long and serious

69
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,720
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:45,690
I went back in one more time.

71
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:46,760
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:48,780
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:49,940
And like the three before it,

74
00:01:49,940 --> 00:01:52,680
the answer was everything looks great.

75
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,560
No loosening, no infection,

76
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:55,780
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:55,780 --> 00:01:57,090
Only this time there

78
00:01:57,090 --> 00:01:58,700
was no new number.

79
00:01:58,700 --> 00:01:59,850
Nobody said

80
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:01,450
give it another six months.

81
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:03,580
There was nothing left to give it.

82
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:04,410
I sat in the parking

83
00:02:04,410 --> 00:02:05,320
lot for a while.

84
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,010
Okay, I thought.

85
00:02:07,010 --> 00:02:08,660
Then explain this.

86
00:02:08,660 --> 00:02:10,750
Anyway, a couple of months back,

87
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,530
I hit my breaking point.

88
00:02:12,530 --> 00:02:14,770
It was around 2:30 in the morning.

89
00:02:14,770 --> 00:02:16,620
Everyone in the house was asleep

90
00:02:16,620 --> 00:02:18,310
and I was downstairs in the recliner

91
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:19,540
with my leg up,

92
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,140
trying to find any angle where

93
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,310
it didn't feel like something

94
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:23,590
was wrapped around my knee

95
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:24,670
and tightening.

96
00:02:24,670 --> 00:02:27,210
My wife didn't know I'd come downstairs.

97
00:02:27,210 --> 00:02:29,600
By then I'd stopped telling her.

98
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:30,670
And I just thought,

99
00:02:30,670 --> 00:02:32,710
is this really my life now?

100
00:02:32,710 --> 00:02:34,700
Thirty-two years, and I park

101
00:02:34,700 --> 00:02:36,270
the machine for good because

102
00:02:36,270 --> 00:02:37,320
of a knee that

103
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,850
looks great on an X-ray?

104
00:02:38,850 --> 00:02:40,160
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,950
So I made myself a promise.

106
00:02:41,950 --> 00:02:42,820
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,510
without looking for an answer.

108
00:02:44,510 --> 00:02:45,710
And when I found one,

109
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:46,770
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:48,360
going through the same thing.

111
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,360
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,410
out and went looking.

113
00:02:50,410 --> 00:02:51,630
Not for a product.

114
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:53,030
For an explanation.

115
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:54,700
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:57,150
the knee replacement group on Facebook,

117
00:02:57,150 --> 00:03:00,260
doctor videos, medical animations.

118
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:01,180
And that's when I found

119
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,520
a video from a physical therapist

120
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:04,130
named Dr.

121
00:03:04,130 --> 00:03:06,290
Steven Salinger, whose own wife

122
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:08,210
had been through exactly this.

123
00:03:08,210 --> 00:03:10,290
But before I say anything else,

124
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:11,610
I want to be straight with you.

125
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:13,830
You've already had something work fast.

126
00:03:13,830 --> 00:03:14,940
The ice.

127
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,510
The first week of a new pill.

128
00:03:16,510 --> 00:03:18,110
The good day after a session.

129
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:19,300
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,430
That's the part nobody warns you about.

131
00:03:21,430 --> 00:03:23,420
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:24,660
It's a preview.

133
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:26,020
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:28,080
you this works fast.

135
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,040
It doesn't.

136
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,780
But if you're willing to be patient,

137
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:31,550
and to look at what's

138
00:03:31,550 --> 00:03:32,870
going on around your new knee

139
00:03:32,870 --> 00:03:34,350
instead of inside it, there

140
00:03:34,350 --> 00:03:36,670
is a real reason it still hurts.

141
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:38,920
And something you can do about it.

142
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,300
Let me explain what he said,

143
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:41,560
because this is what changed

144
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,950
everything for me.

145
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:44,830
He started with the basics.

146
00:03:44,830 --> 00:03:46,260
A knee replacement takes out

147
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:47,940
the worn joint surfaces and puts

148
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:49,440
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,400
That's what stops the arthritis pain

150
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,330
you had before the operation.

151
00:03:53,330 --> 00:03:55,330
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:55,330 --> 00:03:56,770
But then he explained something

153
00:03:56,770 --> 00:03:58,560
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,090
He said,

155
00:03:59,090 --> 00:04:00,530
think about a swollen foot

156
00:04:00,530 --> 00:04:02,030
inside a shoe.

157
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:03,770
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:03,770 --> 00:04:06,230
Your foot is taking up more room,

159
00:04:06,230 --> 00:04:07,820
so everything feels cramped

160
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:09,690
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:09,690 --> 00:04:10,710
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:12,440
in a limited space with living

163
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:14,460
tissue packed all around it.

164
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,510
To put that knee in, the surgeon

165
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:18,290
had to work through that tissue.

166
00:04:18,290 --> 00:04:21,630
Afterwards it gets inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:21,630 --> 00:04:23,300
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,020
But in some people that swelling can

169
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:27,920
stay switched on far longer than expected.

170
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,480
And swollen tissue takes up more

171
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:31,420
room than calm tissue does.

172
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:32,850
So when you bend,

173
00:04:32,850 --> 00:04:34,560
that tissue gets compressed.

174
00:04:34,560 --> 00:04:35,870
When you straighten,

175
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:37,260
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:38,360
That's the band.

177
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:40,490
That's the ache that never quite leaves.

178
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:41,290
And you start being

179
00:04:41,290 --> 00:04:42,410
the one who says,

180
00:04:42,410 --> 00:04:42,970
you go ahead.

181
00:04:42,970 --> 00:04:44,170
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:45,690
And that's exactly why so much

183
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:48,470
of what I'd tried hadn't worked.

184
00:04:48,470 --> 00:04:50,440
Physical therapy strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,600
around the knee.

186
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,330
Worth doing,

187
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:53,430
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:54,890
It does nothing about tissue

189
00:04:54,890 --> 00:04:56,110
taking up room.

190
00:04:56,110 --> 00:04:57,310
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:57,310 --> 00:04:59,460
the nerve carrying the signal.

192
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:02,140
It doesn't touch what's generating it.

193
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:03,800
But when that irritated tissue

194
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:05,400
finally calms down,

195
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:06,900
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:08,990
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:08,990 --> 00:05:10,890
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:10,890 --> 00:05:13,620
less pressure squeezing the joint.

199
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:15,720
That's what takes the pressure off.

200
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,220
After two years of this,

201
00:05:17,220 --> 00:05:19,150
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:21,190
The problem was never the new knee.

203
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,440
It was the tissue crowded around it.

204
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,050
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:25,050 --> 00:05:27,730
Once you've felt it, that's the word.

206
00:05:27,730 --> 00:05:29,210
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:29,210 --> 00:05:31,470
compression braces, creams,

208
00:05:31,470 --> 00:05:33,270
half of Amazon really,

209
00:05:33,270 --> 00:05:34,690
and all any of it gave me

210
00:05:34,690 --> 00:05:35,900
was an hour.

211
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:36,980
I even looked at going

212
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:38,930
to a clinic for the light therapy.

213
00:05:38,930 --> 00:05:40,990
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:40,990 --> 00:05:42,770
with nothing covered by insurance,

215
00:05:42,770 --> 00:05:44,140
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:45,210
Then one night I went

217
00:05:45,210 --> 00:05:46,480
back to that knee replacement

218
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:48,210
group and actually read it.

219
00:05:48,210 --> 00:05:49,530
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:51,140
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:53,430
comparing notes on stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:55,140
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:55,140 --> 00:05:56,870
And no matter how far I scrolled,

224
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:58,670
the same thing kept coming up.

225
00:05:58,670 --> 00:06:00,650
This one device,

226
00:06:00,650 --> 00:06:02,150
and people saying it was the first

227
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:03,750
thing that made a difference.

228
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:06,010
And before anyone jumps in thinking,

229
00:06:06,010 --> 00:06:07,330
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:07,330 --> 00:06:08,660
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:08,660 --> 00:06:10,490
let me shut that down right now.

232
00:06:10,490 --> 00:06:11,970
I'm only here because I made myself

233
00:06:11,970 --> 00:06:13,960
a promise at 2:30 in the morning

234
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:14,900
that if I ever found

235
00:06:14,900 --> 00:06:16,030
something that helped,

236
00:06:16,030 --> 00:06:17,630
I'd say so.

237
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:19,390
It's called the KenRelief Red

238
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:21,010
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:21,010 --> 00:06:23,090
At first glance I didn't buy it.

240
00:06:23,090 --> 00:06:24,180
It looked like the cheap

241
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:25,970
knee sleeves off Amazon

242
00:06:25,970 --> 00:06:27,690
that did nothing for me.

243
00:06:27,690 --> 00:06:29,660
But I went to their website anyway,

244
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,560
just to see what all

245
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,950
the fuss was about.

246
00:06:31,950 --> 00:06:33,550
It's the same red light therapy

247
00:06:33,550 --> 00:06:35,750
clinics charge $200 a session

248
00:06:35,750 --> 00:06:38,010
for, off machines that cost

249
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:39,580
fifty thousand dollars,

250
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:40,560
in a wrap you plug

251
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:42,100
into the wall at home.

252
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:43,940
Two hundred and forty lights.

253
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,850
Red at 660 nanometers

254
00:06:45,850 --> 00:06:48,180
and near-infrared at 850,

255
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:50,740
run together for the strongest effect.

256
00:06:50,740 --> 00:06:52,220
Four strength levels.

257
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:54,530
A five to thirty minute timer.

258
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:56,540
Then I saw the guarantee.

259
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,140
Ninety days.

260
00:06:58,140 --> 00:07:00,600
Results or your money back,

261
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:03,190
no questions, no store credit,

262
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:05,340
and you don't even send it back.

263
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:07,720
No physical therapist ever gave me ninety

264
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,380
days to change my mind.

265
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,680
There wasn't much to lose,

266
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,150
so I ordered it.

267
00:07:12,150 --> 00:07:13,800
Two of them, actually.

268
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,730
Only the right knee was replaced,

269
00:07:15,730 --> 00:07:17,950
but you favor the leg that hurts,

270
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:19,890
and I'd done it for two years.

271
00:07:19,890 --> 00:07:22,050
The left one was carrying the difference.

272
00:07:22,050 --> 00:07:22,980
When it came,

273
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:25,170
I strapped it on expecting nothing,

274
00:07:25,170 --> 00:07:26,530
because I'd been let down too

275
00:07:26,530 --> 00:07:28,350
many times to get excited.

276
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,020
What I felt was warmth.

277
00:07:30,020 --> 00:07:32,230
Not a heating pad kind of hot.

278
00:07:32,230 --> 00:07:34,280
More like it was coming from inside

279
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:36,590
the knee and spreading around it.

280
00:07:36,590 --> 00:07:37,840
And that was it.

281
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:39,530
That was the whole experience.

282
00:07:39,530 --> 00:07:40,550
When I took it off,

283
00:07:40,550 --> 00:07:41,200
I'll be honest,

284
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:43,140
nothing dramatic had happened.

285
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:44,710
And after what that video said,

286
00:07:44,710 --> 00:07:46,860
that's exactly what I expected.

287
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:47,650
What was different

288
00:07:47,650 --> 00:07:48,870
was that for the first

289
00:07:48,870 --> 00:07:50,300
time in two years

290
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:52,240
I'd done something for my knee

291
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,780
instead of to it.

292
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:54,760
Twenty minutes,

293
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:56,130
in my own chair.

294
00:07:56,130 --> 00:07:57,770
No drive, no copay.

295
00:07:57,770 --> 00:07:59,340
They say twenty minutes.

296
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:00,660
I did thirty,

297
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:01,960
twice a day,

298
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:04,440
lowest setting that first week.

299
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,170
I put it on the calendar.

300
00:08:06,170 --> 00:08:08,520
Once before work, once after supper.

301
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:09,680
The first week,

302
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:10,580
I couldn't have told

303
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:12,680
you if anything was happening.

304
00:08:12,680 --> 00:08:13,570
I tried not to get

305
00:08:13,570 --> 00:08:14,710
my hopes up.

306
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:16,400
I'd had things help for a week

307
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:17,680
and then stop.

308
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:19,030
But somewhere in the second week

309
00:08:19,030 --> 00:08:20,200
I noticed I'd come down

310
00:08:20,200 --> 00:08:22,250
the stairs without holding the rail.

311
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:23,620
I hadn't decided to.

312
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:24,600
I just did it,

313
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,860
then stopped halfway down

314
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:27,380
because I realized.

315
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:28,760
By the end of the fourth week

316
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,840
I'd slept through the night

317
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,580
four times running.

318
00:08:31,580 --> 00:08:32,580
I stood at the counter

319
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:33,950
and finished making dinner

320
00:08:33,950 --> 00:08:35,970
without looking for the stool.

321
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:37,610
None of that is dramatic.

322
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:38,690
All of it was gone

323
00:08:38,690 --> 00:08:40,120
for two years.

324
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:41,740
A few weeks later my wife asked

325
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:42,700
if I wanted to walk

326
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:44,370
the long way around the block.

327
00:08:44,370 --> 00:08:45,420
And for the first time

328
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:46,130
in two years,

329
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:47,220
I said yes.

330
00:08:47,220 --> 00:08:49,160
I wanted to understand why,

331
00:08:49,160 --> 00:08:50,520
so I read the whole thing.

332
00:08:50,520 --> 00:08:52,280
It comes down to four steps.

333
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:53,240
One.

334
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,790
The tissue around a new knee can

335
00:08:54,790 --> 00:08:57,610
stay inflamed long after surgery is over.

336
00:08:57,610 --> 00:08:58,430
Two.

337
00:08:58,430 --> 00:09:00,430
Inflamed tissue holds extra fluid,

338
00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:01,320
so it takes up more

339
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:02,700
room than it should.

340
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:03,350
Three.

341
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:05,140
There's only so much room in there.

342
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:06,890
Bending compresses it.

343
00:09:06,890 --> 00:09:08,330
Straightening pulls it tight.

344
00:09:08,330 --> 00:09:09,770
That's the squeeze.

345
00:09:09,770 --> 00:09:10,620
Four.

346
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:12,340
Red and near-infrared light have been

347
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:14,550
studied for calming that inflammation,

348
00:09:14,550 --> 00:09:15,790
so the swelling and the pressure

349
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,250
can come down with it.

350
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:18,670
In a randomized trial,

351
00:09:18,670 --> 00:09:20,460
patients given light therapy after

352
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:21,720
a knee replacement

353
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,940
had less pain,

354
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:24,000
less swelling

355
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,330
and better early movement than

356
00:09:25,330 --> 00:09:26,680
those who weren't.

357
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:29,480
A 2025 review said the same,

358
00:09:29,480 --> 00:09:30,640
and was clear the evidence

359
00:09:30,640 --> 00:09:31,850
is still limited.

360
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:33,380
I probably sound like a broken

361
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,930
record to my family and the guys

362
00:09:34,930 --> 00:09:36,120
on my crew.

363
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,910
But after two years of doing everything

364
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:39,920
I was told and getting nowhere,

365
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,030
you have no idea what it's

366
00:09:41,030 --> 00:09:42,490
like to sleep through the night,

367
00:09:42,490 --> 00:09:43,820
say yes to the walk,

368
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,410
and get my life back.

369
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:46,880
So take it from me.

370
00:09:46,880 --> 00:09:48,430
Don't spend another year waiting

371
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:49,830
for it to settle.

372
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:51,830
Don't spend two hundred a session.

373
00:09:51,830 --> 00:09:53,420
More than ten thousand people

374
00:09:53,420 --> 00:09:54,520
with pain after a knee

375
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:57,230
replacement have already tried this.

376
00:09:57,230 --> 00:09:59,160
Some had it worse than I did.

377
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,450
You can get the KenRelief

378
00:10:00,450 --> 00:10:02,130
wrap from their website,

379
00:10:02,130 --> 00:10:03,660
with a discount link

380
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:05,620
and ninety days to try it.

381
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:07,550
If it doesn't do anything for you,

382
00:10:07,550 --> 00:10:08,860
you get your money back

383
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:10,310
and you keep the wrap.

384
00:10:10,310 --> 00:10:11,990
They only release so many

385
00:10:11,990 --> 00:10:13,410
at that price.

386
00:10:13,410 --> 00:10:14,910
If it's still there,

387
00:10:14,910 --> 00:10:15,780
get one,

388
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:17,320
and stop the squeeze.
